{"id":"2101641510559072682","authorId":"66804351","createdAt":"2026-09-20T11:55:57.000Z","type":"quote","refId":"2101393622138519695","lang":"en","text":"It has always been, and will always be true that immigrants (documented and otherwise) are a net gain for our economy.  They are working age, they come here to work and they pay taxes.  The inverse of is also true: Trump’s anti-immigrant policies slow US economic growth. https://t.co/fHCw4yPSrk","capturedAt":"2026-09-20T12:01:54.873Z","metricsAtCapture":{"likes":4,"retweets":1,"replies":0,"quotes":0},"quoted":{"id":"2101393622138519695","authorId":"1938013934604414976","handle":"David_Charts2","text":"CBO estimated Biden's immigration surge as a nearly $1 trillion deficit/debt reducer over a decade.\nhttps://t.co/bocSXfdXeD https://t.co/QvWa38oiXO","metrics":{"likes":932,"retweets":219,"replies":19,"quotes":17,"impressions":60470},"createdAt":"2026-09-19T19:30:56.000Z","source":{"version":1,"url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2101393622138519695","textField":"text","raw":{"text":"CBO estimated Biden's immigration surge as a nearly $1 trillion deficit/debt reducer over a decade.\nhttps://t.co/bocSXfdXeD https://t.co/QvWa38oiXO","entities":{"urls":[{"description":"An increase in immigration over the 2021–2026 period boosts federal revenues as well as mandatory spending and interest on the debt in CBO’s baseline projections, lowering deficits, on net, by $0.9 trillion over the 2024–2034 period.","display_url":"cbo.gov/publication/60…","end":123,"expanded_url":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/60165","images":[{"height":400,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2099502680871768064/TwdG2n-m?format=jpg&name=orig","width":800},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2099502680871768064/TwdG2n-m?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":100,"status":200,"title":"Effects of the Immigration Surge on the Federal Budget and the Economy","unwound_url":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/60165","url":"https://t.co/bocSXfdXeD"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/QvWa38oiXO","end":147,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/David_Charts2/status/2101393622138519695/photo/1","media_key":"3_2101393495671939073","start":124,"url":"https://t.co/QvWa38oiXO"}]},"created_at":"2026-09-19T19:30:56.000Z","conversation_id":"2101393622138519695","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2101393622138519695"]},"urls":[{"field":"entities","url":"https://t.co/bocSXfdXeD","expandedUrl":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/60165","unwoundUrl":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/60165","displayUrl":"cbo.gov/publication/60…","start":100,"end":123},{"field":"entities","url":"https://t.co/QvWa38oiXO","expandedUrl":"https://x.com/David_Charts2/status/2101393622138519695/photo/1","displayUrl":"pic.x.com/QvWa38oiXO","start":124,"end":147}],"references":[]}},"source":{"version":1,"url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2101641510559072682","textField":"text","raw":{"text":"It has always been, and will always be true that immigrants (documented and otherwise) are a net gain for our economy.  They are working age, they come here to work and they pay taxes.  The inverse of is also true: Trump’s anti-immigrant policies slow US economic growth. https://t.co/fHCw4yPSrk","entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/david_charts2/…","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/david_charts2/status/2101393622138519695","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/fHCw4yPSrk"}]},"created_at":"2026-09-20T11:55:57.000Z","conversation_id":"2101641510559072682","referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2101393622138519695","type":"quoted"}],"edit_history_tweet_ids":["2101641510559072682"]},"urls":[{"field":"entities","url":"https://t.co/fHCw4yPSrk","expandedUrl":"https://twitter.com/david_charts2/status/2101393622138519695","displayUrl":"x.com/david_charts2/…","start":272,"end":295}],"references":[{"id":"2101393622138519695","type":"quoted","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2101393622138519695","createdAt":"2026-09-19T19:30:56.000Z","source":{"version":1,"url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/210139